      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{12-3y}{6}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12-3y}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{12}{6}-\\frac{3y}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{12}{6}-\\frac{3}{6}\\cdot y & = \\\\ 2-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot y & = \\\\ 2-\\frac{y}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
